overview:
THE FORMAT, in full — a flat object of key to text, and nothing else:

{
  "menu.start": "Start Game",
  "menu.quit": "Quit",
  "hud.greeting": "Welcome back, {0}!"
}

One file is ONE language; the importer asks you which locale code it belongs to, because the file does not say. Nested objects are flattened with dots, so the equally common

{ "menu": { "start": "Start Game", "quit": "Quit" } }

produces exactly the same keys — which is what lets a file exported from a web translation tool drop straight in.
